<title>USA: Fruit of the Loom files $850 mln shelf.</title>
<headline>Fruit of the Loom files $850 mln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fruit of the Loom Inc filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $850 million in debt securities, preferred stock and Class A common shares.</p>
<p>The Chicago-based underwear maker said it doesn't have any specific plans for the net proceeds but anticipates that they may be used for general corporate purposes, including funding working capital needs, capital expenditures and repaying outstanding debt.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the filing.</p>
</text>
